        <tr>
          <th>Stage</th>
          <th>What it actually involves</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {degreeRows.map((item) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Stage"><strong>{item.stage}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="What it actually involves">{item.detail}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    The BA and general MA stages are shared by almost every track below. The branch point is your MA specialisation and, for clinical work only, the additional RCI-regulated course and registration step.
  </p>

  <h2 id="zones">The 3 Regulation Zones test before you pick a track</h2>

  <p>
    Instead of asking "is psychology a good career," a sharper question is which Regulation Zone you are actually willing to work inside. Call it <strong>the 3 Regulation Zones</strong>: the Regulated Zone (clinical work, RCI-gated), the Recommended Zone (counselling, no legal mandate but qualification still matters), and the Open Zone (organizational psychology, research, UX research, and analytics, where no licensing body exists at all).
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    {zoneCards.map((item) => (
      <div class:list={['compare-card', item.label === 'Regulated Zone' ? 'compare-card--gold' : 'compare-card--teal']}>
        <div class="compare-card__label">{item.label}</div>
        <ul>
          {item.items.map((line) => (
            <li>{line}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    Most people who say "psychology has no scope in India" are only picturing the Regulated Zone - the long clinical timeline - and never test whether the Recommended or Open Zone fits their actual goals better. Naming your zone honestly, before picking a track, is the single fastest way to avoid years spent training for a rule that does not even apply to the work you actually want to do.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tracks">The 6 real psychology career tracks in India</h2>

  <p>
    With the zones named, here are the six tracks themselves - what each one actually pays at entry, mid-career, and senior level, and which zone it sits inside.
  </p>

  <div class="tracks-grid">
    {trackCards.map((item) => (
      <div class:list={['track-card', `track-card--${item.tone}`]}>
